# Environment for switchtender-witness.service. systemd reads it as root before the service starts.
#
# Install it as /etc/switchtender-witness/switchtender-witness.env, owner root, mode 0600, and fill
# in both values there. The filled-in copy never leaves the droplet and is never committed. The
# witness signing key is never set here: it lives only in witness-key.json in the key directory.

# SWITCHTENDER_WITNESS_TOKEN is the bearer token the cross-server /witness routes require. Set it
# even though the API listens on loopback, because the tunnel forwards the public hostname to
# loopback. Generate it on the droplet with: openssl rand -hex 32
SWITCHTENDER_WITNESS_TOKEN=

# SWITCHTENDER_WITNESS_NOTIFY_SLACK is the Slack incoming webhook URL for #switchtender. Every
# refusal and every note about an enrolled install is posted there, silent_install included. The
# URL is the credential, which is why it is set here and not on the command line, where every
# process on the host could read it.
SWITCHTENDER_WITNESS_NOTIFY_SLACK=
